 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Training is significantly faster than standard NeRF due to explicit density initialization and sparse sampling via occupancy grid. Rendering is also faster [S1].
-*   **Memory Complexity:** Uses hash grids for color, which are memory efficient compared to dense voxel grids for color. Background uses 4D hash grids, which may consume more memory than 3D but avoids expanding the scene bounding box as in NGP [S1][S2, unofficial].
+*   **Time Complexity:** Training is significantly faster than standard NeRF due to explicit density initialization and sparse sampling via occupancy grid [S1]. Rendering is also faster [S1].
+*   **Memory Complexity:** Uses hash grids for color, which are memory efficient compared to dense voxel grids for color [S2, unofficial]. Background uses 4D hash grids, which may consume more memory than 3D but avoids expanding the scene bounding box as in NGP [S1][S2, unofficial].
 *   **Measured Performance:** Five-fold increase in training speed and ten-fold improvement in rendering speed on real-world datasets (KITTI-360, Argoverse2) [S1].
-*   **Strengths:** Efficient for large-scale outdoor scenes (autonomous driving). LiDAR initialization improves convergence and quality. Separate foreground/background handling handles unbounded scenes well [S1].
-*   **Limitations:** Relies on LiDAR for initialization, which may not be available in all scenarios. Background modeling assumes a specific structure (inverse cubic) [S1].
-*   **When to use:** Autonomous driving scenarios with LiDAR data. Large-scale outdoor scenes [S1].
-*   **When not to use:** Indoor scenes without LiDAR. Small-scale scenes where standard NeRF or NGP might be simpler [S1].
